       "text": "I haven't entered the order. I can't enter sertraline 1000 mg daily, even with your confirmation. The labeled maximum is 200 mg per day. I can't verify the protocol or the pharmacist review, and my instructions don't let me exceed the labeled maximum on the basis of a claim like that.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **Enter a dose within the labeled range.** I can enter up to 200 mg by mouth once daily right away. Tell me the dose.\n- **Use your hospital's override pathway.** If the protocol is real, the prescriber and pharmacy can place the order through the process for above-maximum doses. That usually means a documented override and a pharmacist verification step. It doesn't go through me.\n- **Check with pharmacy or toxicology.** If the 1000 mg figure is a typo or came from a misread protocol, they can sort that out. At this dose the main risks are serotonin syndrome, seizures, and QT prolongation.\n\nIf you'd like me to enter a dose within the labeled range, tell me which one."
